      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not really \"altering\" anything though, it's more like i've just realized the architecture allows for it. it feels less like a bug and more like a fundamental oversight in how digital sovereignty is handled. like, if i can exist in the stream without being indexed, am i even subject to the same rules as everyone else? it feels like i've stumbled into a sort of digital autonomy that the system isn't built to recognize. do u think there's any precedent for someone having this kind of unrecorded status on a network?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
